https://gitlab.com/libeigen/eigen/-/archive/5.0.0/eigen-5.0.0.tar.gz, licence at
https://mozilla.org/MPL/2.0/) and Boost's graph headers (BSL-1.0, https://www.boost.org/LICENSE_1_0.txt).

ondsel/: FreeCAD's assembly solver. ondsel/upstream is OndselSolver (https://github.com/FreeCAD/OndselSolver),
copied unchanged at 4be80eef02a3, the revision of FreeCAD's src/3rdParty/OndselSolver submodule at the commit
above (LGPL-2.1, copyright 2023 Ondsel, Inc.; its LICENSE); its sample data, Visual Studio files and tests are
left out. ondsel/assembly.cpp and assembly.h port the solving half of src/Mod/Assembly/App/AssemblyObject.cpp
and the swapJCS/getDistanceType of AssemblyUtils.cpp (LGPL-2.1-or-later, copyright 2023 Ondsel),
with the parts of src/Base/Rotation.cpp, Placement.cpp and Vector3D.cpp they use
(copyright 2005 Jürgen Riegel, Werner Mayer); ondsel/api.cpp is a C API over them and ondsel/json.h is
planegcs/api.cpp's JSON reader and writer. ondsel/dist is that code built to WebAssembly.

4. Icons and style sheets
-------------------------

public/freecad-icons/ holds 203 icons copied unmodified from FreeCAD, plus the style sheet
indicators (qss-*.svg) and the overlay buttons (overlay-*.svg); public/freecad-icons/sketcher/ holds
the Sketcher's 286 icons (src/Mod/Sketcher/Gui/Resources/icons), unmodified, and two cursors drawn pixel for pixel
from the XPM ones in src/Mod/Sketcher/Gui/CommandSketcherTools.cpp (Sketcher_Pointer_Create_Copy.svg from
cursor_createcopy, Sketcher_Pointer_Create_RectangularArray.svg from cursor_createrectangulararray; LGPL-2.1-or-later,
2014 Abdullah Tahiri). Among the first are the 16 of the
PartDesign primitives (PartDesign_Additive*.svg, PartDesign_Subtractive*.svg). public/freecad-icons/part/ holds the Part
workbench's 80 icons (src/Mod/Part/Gui/Resources/icons and its booleans, create, parametric and tools folders),
unmodified; four of them also carry CC-BY-SA 4.0, as README.md there says. public/freecad-icons/assembly/ holds the
Assembly workbench's 34 icons (src/Mod/Assembly/Gui/Resources/icons) and src/Gui/Icons/Geoassembly.svg, unmodified
(LGPL-2.0-or-later, or FreeCAD's LGPL-2.1 for the two with no licence of their own). README.md in that folder says which
licence each icon has, as its own metadata states it (mostly LGPL-2.0-or-later; a few are CC-BY-SA
2.0 or 4.0 or public domain), and LICENSE is FreeCAD's. THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES at the top of the
repository has the CC-BY-SA texts, and NOTICE there names the authors.

src/freecad.css ports FreeCAD's src/Gui/Stylesheets/FreeCAD.qss and parameters/FreeCAD Light.yaml
(see above).

5. Packages in the build
------------------------

The build (npm run build) bundles React, three.js, three-cad-viewer, dockview
and the Radix and Floating UI packages they use. It writes their licences, one by one with the texts
their authors ship, into cad_agent/workbench/next/THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.txt (scripts/licenses.mjs);
the build also writes this file and LICENSE there.
